  Source revision: 3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464. Parent author:
  hairer-codex-existence-20261111.

  <section|One prescription><label|one-prescription>

  <verbatim|ope-prescription.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OPE/Splitting/{Basis,Needle,Legacy,Detector}.lean>.
  Principal declarations are <verbatim|YM.OPE.reachReads>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.Prescription.startRows>, <verbatim|nextRows>,
  <verbatim|chosen>, <verbatim|highVan>, <verbatim|reading>, <verbatim|ope>,
  <verbatim|insertOne>. The proof preserves finite dual spanning by actual
  correlation tests, the corrected quotient lift S-RBS, old/new
  biorthogonality, freezing both needles and test combinations, and the
  relative-origin separated raw evaluation. Independent review passed
  b332b2c3cd21bc6224659e9f1452b8c37a81a451e907f94728ab5ecdbdd4bd78.

  <section|Covariant homogeneous coefficients><label|covariant-homogeneous-coefficients>

  <verbatim|ope-homogeneous.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OPE/Orbits/{Port,Spin,Average,Real,Cuts,Fresh,Stars,System}.lean>.
  Principal declarations: <verbatim|compact_dock>,
  <verbatim|smooth_orbit_row>, <verbatim|averageV>, <verbatim|average_fixes>,
  <verbatim|average_rotation>, <verbatim|checkReal>,
  <verbatim|checkReal_fixed>, <verbatim|Reader.liftOne_affinity>,
  <verbatim|knife_apply>, <verbatim|reconstruct>, <verbatim|kills_lower>,
  <verbatim|knife_mem>, <verbatim|fresh>, <verbatim|rotate_knife>,
  <verbatim|real_knife>, <verbatim|basis_exists_c>,
  <verbatim|Reader.assemble>, <verbatim|filtered_packet>,
  <verbatim|packet_read>. It proves orbit-open/smooth Haar averaging with
  input/output rotations, conjugation averaging, fixed singleton and
  inclusion maps, recursive exact homogeneous projections, invariant
  complement spaces, real channel bases, and packet/truncation identities. It
  does not yet prove quantitative errors. Independent local review passed
  SHA256 621f8e99c7f2dce813333c8fbe022cfabef7f47a457ada36e707f08aab62b7e7.

  All machine review fields remain null. No complete OPE or construction
  assertion is inferred from these finite-dimensional arguments.

  <section|Quantitative transfer to homogeneous
  coefficients><label|quantitative-transfer-to-homogeneous-coefficients>

  <verbatim|ope-estimates.tex> follows the fixed-exterior specialization a=1,
  b=c=0 of <verbatim|Exchange/{Arrangement,Regime}.lean> and
  <verbatim|Orbits/{Quotes,Clearance,Rent,Receipts,Fee,Gain,Separated}.lean>,
  with the rate definition in <verbatim|Rate.lean>. It proves the rotated
  finite-test error identity, bounded-label finite-basis extension,
  uniformity over rotations, conjugated comparison with J H_D,
  projected-shadow bridge, higher-degree coefficient estimate and exact
  raw-plus-correction remainder. A violating sequence proves uniformity over
  geometry and phases. The raw coefficient, full discrepancy and separated
  spectator estimates remain explicit inputs. Independent local review passed
  SHA256 6ffbdcd702e5b097338182750dbf8af81fef644628e72f899bd98acffcfe0760.

  Next producer reads: <verbatim|Schemes/{Travel,Rearrange,Corridor}.lean>
  and <verbatim|Interpolate/Education.lean>; the source first proves
  estimates on a fine grid (<verbatim|Schemes/Ladder.lean>), extends them by
  derivative-controlled interpolation, then lets the intermediate logarithmic
  scales approach the cluster scale. This producer is not yet proved by the
  preceding chapter.

  <section|Grid matching and grading interpolation><label|grid-matching-and-grading-interpolation>

  <verbatim|ope-grid.tex> is an author draft of the fixed-clearance exterior
  specialization of <verbatim|Schemes/{Read,Ladder,Corridor,Travel,Rearrange}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Interpolate/{Chart,Leap,Corridor,Education}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Eye/{Cloud,Extract,Remit}.lean>, and <verbatim|Height.lean> (full
  reads). It proves selection of logarithmic mesh levels under Gentle,
  coordinate-generic rounding via residues (empty forbidden set), stability
  of the scale corridor, channel estimates from a lower-filtration
  approximation, finite high-horizon remainder decomposition, descending
  induction through derivative grades, and removal of intermediate-scale
  losses. It preserves the source's grid-to-all-point route, rather than
  assuming an arbitrary-point matching estimate. Principal declarations:
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.found>, <verbatim|YM.OPE.Cloud.screened>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.cloud_jump>, <verbatim|YM.OPE.at_grade>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.det_cost>, <verbatim|YM.OPE.grid_coeff>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.grid_remainder>, <verbatim|YM.OPE.leap_cost>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.interpolated>, <verbatim|YM.OPE.common_rate>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.early_rate>. Actual cutoff matching, filtration-distance
  and rough correlation production remain explicit inputs. Independent local
  review passed current SHA256 7aa64011922fc4318f6f13a542187a0865afeb2ebed19792b4069f4b5857b98b.

  Further full producer reads: <verbatim|Columns/{SectorCost,Limit}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Prices/{Circuit,Space}.lean>, and <verbatim|Sweep/Camp.lean>.
  <verbatim|for_plot> selects a SAME-match sublimit from <verbatim|PriceAt>;
  <verbatim|at_grade> relies on <verbatim|Columns.limit_cap>, not a
  bare-vector low-subspace assertion. <verbatim|funding> calls
  <verbatim|ManyCopies.joins>, which uses <verbatim|Ballet>,
  <verbatim|Created.bridge> and <verbatim|bequeathed>. These substantive
  estimates are not discharged by rate arithmetic. Guessed files
  Prices/{Data,Bound,Budget}.lean do not exist and were not read.

  <section|Centered prices and physical filtration, 11 November
  continuation><label|centered-prices-and-physical-filtration-11-november-continuation>

  <verbatim|ope-phase-prices.tex> supplies two-scale mixed planted estimates,
  simultaneous coarse/fine origins (explicit finite residue counts and 10/6
  room constants), integer even replicas, moving-label finite-cutoff limits,
  ground-algebra even moments and full-support phase bounds, generic
  spectator approximation, engineering rates with
  0\<leqslant\>a\<leqslant\>b, and transfer of the entire matched
  discrepancy. Fully read sources at the unit pin:
  <verbatim|YM/OPE/Cards/{Literal,Scale,Mix,Pressure}.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/OPE/Eye/{Fleeting,Admire,Civic,Fast}.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/Work/B17.lean>, and <verbatim|YM/Work/B15.lean> for
  address/span conventions. Independent stronger-agent local pass at SHA256
  <verbatim|09ad65853eda7485300a4d2d5a4ed60f0cd907bb4b7bfb89c8674a17a3b3d17b>.
  Requires actual centered bound and finite-cutoff matched label/price; it
  does not produce them.

  <verbatim|ope-filtration.tex> is a new draft, pending independent review.
  It proves the low-coordinate cone and transverse bound, repeated plane
  cancellation, reference-distance estimate with exponent
  d\<minus\>e\<minus\>1, compact normalized-test identification, and
  resulting physical-filtration distance/rate. Fully read:
  <verbatim|YM/OPE/Columns/{Accounts,Cone,Plane,SectorCost,Reannounce,ExtensionCost,Limit}.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/Dash/Limits.lean>, <verbatim|YM/Bid/Drops.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/Push/RELAY_DIFFERENCE/RawTop.lean>, and
  <verbatim|YM/MergeProof/Portions.lean>. Qualified central declarations:
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.Columns.step_expand>, <verbatim|step_transverse>,
  <verbatim|quotient_issue>, <verbatim|limit_cap>, <verbatim|whole_origin>,
  <verbatim|fare_rate>, <verbatim|reannounce>, <verbatim|limit_lower>;
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.Columns.ExtensionCost.matched>; <verbatim|YM.Dash.brace>.
  Source read via <verbatim|cat>/<verbatim|rg>; no Lean compilation or axiom
  replay. An exploratory glob <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RelayDifference*> failed
  (actual directory is uppercase <verbatim|RELAY_DIFFERENCE>); subsequent
  exact files above were read.

  Remaining physical-identification inputs are explicit: calibrated
  triangular columns; column/coupling subpower costs; local protected-trial
  comparison <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.onions> through
  <verbatim|persists>/<verbatim|served_dollar>; relay projections and
  null-test comparison; the actual finite match. The article does not
  identify bare low coordinates with the physical filtration by definition,
  nor assume convergence of the transport matrices. Shared literature notes
  supply no precise replacement for this source-specific transport;
  finite-dimensional linear algebra and compactness are proved directly.

  Filtration local review passed after adding explicit divergent level/time
  hypotheses, nonnegative logarithmic scales, and cutoff-dependent purchased
  derivative orders/powers/thresholds. Frozen SHA256:
  <verbatim|de3eb826e348a10fddb6b7be08e73f63389296209fb670f4987a9df91ae77255>.
  The added D01/D02 arguments were checked against the fully read
  <verbatim|YM/Work/D01.lean> and <verbatim|YM/Work/D02.lean>; they discharge
  bounded-reference bare subpower cost and the
  separated-bound-to-smeared-discrepancy step. Actual calibration and local
  comparison/projection production remain.

  New <verbatim|ope-cutoff.tex> draft follows
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.ManyCopies.net_select>,
